+    Some("Company".to_owned())
+} else {
+    group.iter().find_map(|row| row.donor_kind.clone())
+};
```

A retained number now comes from an observation explicitly reporting `Company`. That evidence also determines the group’s kind, satisfying the schema constraint even when an earlier observation reports another kind. Without that evidence, the existing first-reported-kind selection remains.

This follows the Model the Domain principle by keeping company status and its number consistent. Status-absent resolver anchors do not gain an inferred Company status.

